From: VyOS LS1046A Build <build@vyos.io>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:36:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: sfp: fix OEM SFP-H10GB-CU1M part-number match (no
 dash)

Follow-up to this same patch's first version: the EEPROM base
structure checksum quirk added for the OEM 10G DAC module compared
id.base.vendor_pn against "SFP-H10G-B-CU1M" (15 bytes), but the
module's actual EEPROM field reads "SFP-H10GB-CU1M" -- no dash
between "H10G" and "B". The extra dash was a misread of the raw hex
dump's ASCII rendering (dmesg wraps "sfp EE:" lines at 16 bytes, and
the '-' in the *following* row, "-CU1M", visually lined up with the
break between "H10G" and "B" in the row above).

Board-verified via a raw hex dump of the live EEPROM
(vendor_name="OEM"+13 spaces at offset 20, vendor_pn="SFP-H10GB-CU1M"
+ 2 spaces at offset 40): with the wrong 15-byte "SFP-H10G-B-CU1M"
string, memcmp() never matched, oem_h10g_cu1m stayed false, and the
checksum mismatch kept hitting the fatal dev_err()/-EINVAL path --
confirmed on hardware (eth3/eth4 still NO-CARRIER, dmesg still showing
the print_hex_dump'd fatal-path message) after deploying the first
version of this patch. Corrected to the true 14-byte prefix
"SFP-H10GB-CU1M".

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A Build <build@vyos.io>
---
 drivers/net/phy/sfp.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -2391,7 +2391,7 @@ static int sfp_sm_mod_probe(struct sfp *sfp, bool report)
 	}

 	/*
-	 * OEM SFP-H10G-B-CU1M (unbranded 10G DAC) ships with a base-structure
+	 * OEM SFP-H10GB-CU1M (unbranded 10G DAC) ships with a base-structure
 	 * checksum byte that never matches the computed value (observed
 	 * 0xf0 != 0xf3, deterministic across reads/modules, not an I2C
 	 * glitch) -- a firmware/programming defect of this generic module,
@@ -2403,7 +2403,7 @@ static int sfp_sm_mod_probe(struct sfp *sfp, bool report)
 	 * NO-CARRIER forever.
 	 */
 	oem_h10g_cu1m = !memcmp(id.base.vendor_name, "OEM             ", 16) &&
-			!memcmp(id.base.vendor_pn, "SFP-H10G-B-CU1M", 15);
+			!memcmp(id.base.vendor_pn, "SFP-H10GB-CU1M", 14);

 	/* Validate the checksum over the base structure */
 	check = sfp_check(&id.base, sizeof(id.base) - 1);
